      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, my dear friend, let me tell you a tale of the goblin's secret vault. Imagine you have a magical goblin who can turn your precious goblin gold into a glittering, indecipherable sparkle. Now, this goblin is quite clever and can make the sparkle so dazzling that even the most cunning goblin thief can't figure out what it is. But what if another goblin, not so clever, tries to replicate the sparkle by simply copying the goblin's original gold? The thief might get caught, but the sparkle could still be a copy, right?\n\nSo, you see, adding a salt to your password before hashing it is like giving your goblin gold a unique, magical dust that only you and your goblin friend know. Even if the thief tries to replicate the sparkle, without the magical dust, the sparkle won't be the same, and the thief will be left scratching their goblin head in confusion. Salting your password is an extra step, but it's a step that makes your goblin gold sparkle even more uniquely and securely. It's not just an extra step; it's a crucial one for keeping your goblin treasures safe from those pesky goblin thieves.",
